          "text": "# Mork: A Gleam Markdown Parser\n\n**What it does:**\nMork is a Markdown parser built entirely in Gleam, aiming for \"100% spec compliant with Commonmark and eventually to implement all of the GFM Markdown extensions.\"\n\n**API Overview:**\nThe library provides a straightforward workflow:\n1. Parse Markdown content using `mork.parse`\n2. Convert the parsed structure to HTML with `mork.to_html`\n\nThe example demonstrates reading a Markdown file, parsing it, and writing the HTML output:\n```gleam\nlet html = markdown |> mork.parse |> mork.to_html\n```\n\n**Output Format:**\nMork renders to **HTML strings**, not Lustre elements. If you need interactive Gleam components, you'd need to integrate this HTML output separately into a Lustre application.\n\n**Current Status:**\nAll CommonMark specification tests pass. The project supports multiple JavaScript runtimes (Node.js, Deno, Bun) and Erlang, though Erlang requires version 28+ due to PCRE2 dependencies.",
