          "text": "# Lustre Packages for Markdown/Content Rendering\n\nBased on the package index, here are the Lustre-related packages that handle markdown, djot, or content rendering:\n\n1. **jot_to_lustre@1.1.0** - \"Convert jot documents or strings to lustre/element/html elements\". This package enables transformation of jot markup into Lustre components.\n\n2. **jotkey@2.0.0** - \"Convert jot documents to lustre elements. Can convert to custom renderers\". This offers more flexibility by supporting custom renderer implementations for jot content.\n\n3. **glimra@2.0.1** - Described as a \"Zero runtime syntax highlighter for lustre/ssg,\" this package provides syntax highlighting capabilities, potentially useful for rendering code blocks within content.\n\nThese three packages directly address content rendering needs in Lustre applications, with the jot-related packages specifically handling markup conversion and glimra focusing on syntax highlighting for code presentation.",
