          "type": "user",
          "text": "# lustre/ssg/djot Module API\n\nThe `lustre/ssg/djot` module enables rendering of djot documents (a markdown-like format) within Lustre static site generation projects.\n\n## Core Types\n\n**Renderer**: A customizable renderer type that transforms djot document elements into views. The module defines: `\"A renderer for a djot document knows how to turn each block or inline element into some custom view.\"` The renderer handles code blocks, emphasis, headings, links, paragraphs, lists, HTML, strong text, inline code, images, and breaks.\n\n## Key Functions\n\n**default_renderer()**: Provides out-of-the-box Lustre element generation without custom configuration.\n\n**render()**: Processes djot documents using a specified renderer, automatically stripping frontmatter before conversion.\n\n**render_with_metadata()**: Combines rendering with TOML frontmatter extraction, passing metadata to the renderer function. Returns a Result type handling potential TOML parsing errors.\n\n**metadata()**: Parses frontmatter as TOML into a dictionary. `\"If there is _no_ frontmatter, this function returns an empty dictionary.\"` Invalid TOML triggers parse errors.\n\n**frontmatter()**: Extracts text between opening and closing triple-dash markers.\n\n**content()**: Retrieves djot markup by removing frontmatter sections.\n\n## Usage Pattern\n\nDocuments support optional TOML frontmatter using the format:\n```\n---\ntitle = \"value\"\n---\n[djot content]\n```\n\nThis module integrates with the jot v2.0.1 package and supports Lustre element generation or custom view transformations.",
